The integrations below are imported as standard Go modules at upstream paths
because forking them under a different vendor namespace would impose
maintenance overhead without functional benefit:

- github.com/casbin/casbin/v2 — RBAC policy engine
- github.com/casdoor/notify2 — multi-provider notification fan-out
- github.com/casdoor/oss — pluggable object-storage backends (S3, GCS, Azure, etc.)
- github.com/casdoor/casdoor-go-sdk — Go client SDK (aliased as iamsdk)
- github.com/casdoor/go-sms-sender — SMS provider adapters
- github.com/casdoor/gomail/v2 — SMTP send
- github.com/casdoor/ldapserver — LDAP server framework

These imports are mechanical dependencies. Hanzo IAM's data model, API
surface, deployment shape, and operational posture are independent.
